Title: More than £8k raised for family after Sutton Coldfield lake death
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'organiser Helena Swallow', 'Text': 'The family are so very grateful, thank you so much,', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 49}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'An online fundraising page set up to support the family of a boy who died after going missing in a lake has raised more than £8,000 within 48 hours.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 115}}, {'Description': 'A GoFundMe page, which organisers said on Saturday was set up with permission from Daniel\'s parents, would help support the family during a "difficult time".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 144}}, {'Description': 'The fundraiser was initially created with the goal of raising £1,600 but quickly surpassed its target and now has a revised goal of £11,000.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 4, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 125}}, {'Description': 'In an update posted on Sunday, organiser Helena Swallow added the teenager\'s mother was "overwhelmed" with all the support and donations.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 125}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'A young man with dark curly hair against a black background'}]}
